# Web SPA env sample (owned by web-fsd-rework — DEC-002 / DEC-008).
#
# No custom VITE_* keys are required. The SPA uses only Vite built-ins:
#   - import.meta.env.BASE_URL — BrowserRouter basename
#       (dev: "/", production build base: "/vises/")
#   - import.meta.env.DEV — API URL dual-mode
#       (dev: relative "/api" via Vite proxy → 127.0.0.1:8100;
#        prod: same-origin "/vises/api/..." via nginx → Nest)
#
# Compose `web` loads this file via env_file so the path exists. An empty
# key list is valid. Runtime env_file does NOT rewrite baked static assets;
# no Docker ARG/ENV for Vite is needed (Dockerfile unchanged).
#
# This supersedes the per-service-env-files stub-only content policy for
# web/.env.example. Compose env_file path and gitignore stay unchanged.
#
# Before `docker compose up`, ensure web/.env exists (copy is enough):
#   copy web\.env.example web\.env   (Windows)
#   cp web/.env.example web/.env     (Unix)
#
# API/db secrets live in backend/.env — see ../backend/.env.example.
# Compose SPA: http://localhost:8090/vises/
# Host Vite: npm run dev in web/ (built-ins only; no custom env required).
